claim.claim-text:
1. A device for carrying out a setting process for setting a connecting element, the device comprising:
a control device for controlling the setting process in operation;
a setting unit that is attached to a tool carrier and that is movable in a feed direction via a feed unit;
a component carrier fastened opposite the setting unit on the tool carrier and against which the setting unit is moveable in the feed direction, the setting unit comprising:
a hold-down device with the aid of which the workpiece is pressed against the component carrier during operation;
a punch that is moveable in the feed direction relative to the hold-down device for punching a hole in the workpiece; and
a punch sleeve to press the connecting element into the hole;

wherein the component carrier comprises has:
a base body with a component support for the workpiece; and
an embossing sleeve that is displaceably arranged in the base body and moveable against the workpiece during operation, such that in operation a deep-drawn collar is formed around the hole,

wherein the control device is designed such that in operation in a multi-stage setting process, in a first stage, a hole punching and hole forming operation to form the hole with the deep-drawn collar and, in a second stage, a setting process for setting the connecting element takes place, and
wherein no lateral relative movement between the workpiece and the device takes place between the two stages.

15. The device according to claim 10, wherein the control device is set up in such a way that the following steps are carried out:
in an initial position, the workpiece rests on the component support;
the setting unit moves in the feed direction and the hold-down device presses the workpiece against the component support and the hole punching and hole-forming operation is carried out;
the position of the workpiece is fixed by moving in the centering pin;
resetting the setting unit against the feed direction and feeding the connecting element into the setting unit;
feeding the setting unit in the feed direction and pressing in the connecting element into the workpiece; and
returning to a starting position.

16. The device according to claim 15, wherein the control device is configured such that the following steps are carried out during the hole punching and hole forming operation:
the hold-down device moves towards the workpiece until a first fixed stop of the hold-down device comes to rest on a stop surface of the feed unit and the hold-down device is blocked from moving back against the feed direction;
the embossing sleeve is moved upwards against the feed direction and forms the collar;
the hole is punched and a punching slug is removed; and
for punching the hole, an axial forced guidance between the punch sleeve and the punch is released

17. The device according to claim 15, wherein the control device is configured such that the following steps take place between the hole punching/hole forming operation and the setting process for fixing the workpiece:
return stroke of a plunger tube of the feed unit into an intermediate position in which the workpiece is still clamped;
return stroke of the embossing sleeve to a second fixed stop;
moving a centering pin into the hole.

18. A method for setting a connecting element on a workpiece with the aid of a device, which has a setting unit with a hold-down device and a component carrier opposite the setting unit with a component support, the method comprising:
performing a hole punching and hole forming operation in a first stage, in which the workpiece is clamped between the hold-down device and the component support;
punching a hole with the aid of a punch of the setting unit;
moving the punch relative to the hold-down device in the feed direction;
forming a deep-drawn collar surrounding the hole using an embossing sleeve, which is arranged in the component carrier and is moved counter to the feed direction; and
pressing the connecting element into the hole in a second stage with the aid of the setting unit,
wherein between the two stages no lateral relative movement between the workpiece and the device takes place.
